\f1\b ## Overview
\f0\b0 \
This repository contains a series of R scripts in /code used to run the full analysis pipeline.  \
The naming convention of the scripts is (#)_\'85 \
The scripts should be run in numeric order.\
Below we describe the what each script does, the inputs to the scripts, and the outputs\
\
\

\f1\b ## (0)_make_train_and_test_data.R
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script formats the training and testing data\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- all files in ~/data_raw/mutantigen/\
	- ~/data_raw/real_respiratory_data_complete.RDS\
	- ~/data_raw/dfreal_var_attr.RDS\

\f1\b Outputs\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_tc.RDS\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_vac.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/train_real.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 ## (1)_train_model.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script trains the transformer models for M(r,.), M(st,.), M(sv,.) and M(a,.). This scripts takes many hours to run.\

\f1\b Inputs: \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_tc.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_vac.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/train_real.RDS\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- everything in the ~/trained_models folder\
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 ## (2)_forecast_model.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script takes the trained models from (1)_train_model.R and performs the forecasting on the COVID test set. \

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\
	- ~/train_models/ (everything in this folder)\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/output/forecasts.csv\
\
\

\f1\b ## (3)_make_results_and_figs.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script plots most of the figures in the paper.\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\
	- ~/output/forecasts.csv\
	- all the config files in ~/output\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- most of the EPS files in ~/figs\
\
\

\f1\b ## (4)_perform_by_ts_trends.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script performs the necessary analysis to make Figure 16 in the paper\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\
	- ~/output/forecasts.csv\
	- all files in ~/data_raw/ts_phases/\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/figs/phase_of_outbreak.eps\
\
\
\

\f1\b ## (5)_umap_analysis.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script performs UMAP analysis and builds a classifier to make Figure 13\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/trained_models/cfg_all.rds\
	- ~/data_clean/train_real.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_tc.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/figs/prob_syn_tc_by_data_types.eps\
	- ~/figs/prob_syn_tc_allstates.eps\
\
\
\

\f1\b ## (6)_show_mutantigen_stochasticity.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script performs the necessary analysis to make Figure S1.\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- select files in ~/data_raw/mutantigen/out_XX.timeseries\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/figs/mutantigen_stochasticity.eps\
\
\
\

\f1\b ## (7a)_train_models_with_training_subsets.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script fits all transformers to subsets of training data to support the analysis presented in Figures 11 and 12. This file takes many hours to run.\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_tc.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/train_syn_vac.RDS\
	- ~/data_clean/train_real.RDS\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- all the files in ~/trained_models_subsets/\
\
\
\

\f1\b ## (7b)_forecast_model_with_training_subsets.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script performs all the forecasts from all the models made in (7a)_ to support the analysis presented in Figures 11 and 12. This script takes over an hour to run.\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\
	- all files in ~/trained_models_subsets/\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/output/forecasts_model_subsets.csv\
\
\
\
\

\f1\b ## (7c)_make_results_and_figs_training_subsets.R\
Description: 
\f0\b0 \
	- This script performs all the necessary analysis to make Figures 11 and 12.\

\f1\b Inputs: 
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/data_clean/test_covid.RDS\
	- ~/output/forecasts_model_subsets.csv\

\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 \
	- ~/figs/training_subsets_paired_differences.eps\
	- ~/figs/training_subsets_metrics.eps\
}